#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:5
#: 9bdacfa434d146a99b33b4cb54d64fc6
msgid "FPort Receivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:7
#: 0079c39f5caa47df9d9c2cd6707bb52b
msgid "ArduPilot supports FPort/FPort2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:9
#: b33a1d17a85c498cbed28acda90ba11d
msgid "FPort protocol combines SBus RC control information being sent to the autopilot with bi-directional telemetry information to/from the autopilot on a single wire high baud rate bus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:11
#: a4dabdf52ca645ba908dd3143624995b
msgid "Many FRSky X series and R series receivers have this capability, either natively or with firmware upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:13
#: 71e12ee628184b898eb4196f8072b5e7
msgid "Connection to the autopilot and configuration varies from autopilot to autopilot since their UART capabilities vary. Most F4 cpu based autopilots do not have controllable inverters in front of the UART TX and RX, and require either an external bi-directional inverter, as SPort connections do or the use of the \"un-inverted FPort pad/pin\" some receivers provide since the FPort protocol has opposite signaling levels than normal UART operation. Most F7 and H7 autopilots, on the other hand, have internal inverters, and can be directly connected from the receiver's FPort to their UARTs TX input line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:16
#: 59f64c9b95774be8a15ded688ebaae59
msgid "ArduPilot supports both 16 and 24 channels FPort2 but telemetry is enabled only for 16 channels mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:19
#: da161e1392a141ca80e5861eab33761f
msgid "Telemetry protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:21
#: b573aa467d794c35ab7bd19d596211ac
msgid "ArduPilot will send telemetry data to the receiver over Fport using the :ref:`Passthrough telemetry <common-frsky-passthrough>` protocol. To get sensors to show up in OpenTX you have to install and enable a script which can display Passthrough telemetry, such as  :ref:`Yaapu FrSky Telemetry Script for OpenTX<common-frsky-yaapu>`. Otherwise the only sensor that will be discovered would be GPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:24
#: bcf6eaa51b2a4628b858e9590aaaea1e
msgid "Connection Diagrams"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:26
#: 7f78692285d44943bd919a079de138bb
msgid "See :ref:`common-connecting-sport-fport` for connection diagrams."
msgstr ""

