#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:42
#: 9dba894c0b5b4f9da4cd40789f6862a7
msgid "F4 based autopilots using an \"un-inverted FPort\" output from the receiver can connect it to any UART's TX pin with the configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:45
#: 1befd9fbaaa84438bf3407aaec626f51
msgid "``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` = 4 (Half Duplex), or = 132 (Half Duplex, TX Pull-up) if receiver does not have sufficient drive on the \"un-inverted\" output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:48
#: a414692914d54101b77f82622161cb1a
msgid "F4 based autopilots cannot use the RX pin with an \"un-inverted FPort\" output since the SWAP capability is only available in F7/H7 based autopilots and Half Duplex requires connection the UART TX pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:51
#: f19b0c2a65a24816afef40cb99150602
msgid "F7/H7 based autopilots can directly connect to the TX pin of any UART and use this configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:53
#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:59
#: e8b7ab0270974697816427633b724565
#: f891647f569640b39b95d5506fc63bb2
msgid "``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` =23"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:54
#: 616c636fa56547f4ae1a66ab2ec22414
msgid "``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` =  7 (invert TX/RX, Half Duplex) if using \"un-inverted\" FPort signal, then = 4 since inversion is not required)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:57
#: 2281e5d857de4f23840b241d62fbcc99
msgid "OR to the RX pin:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:60
#: 27cce16d896748b2913e2db573910c1e
msgid "``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` =  15 (invert TX/RX,Half Duplex, SWAP TX/RX pins)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:64
#: 5733a5a7d5024f0790463ea98365fe71
msgid "Some F7/H7 autopilots have level/shifters on their UARTs that cause a delay in Half Duplex operation, like CubeOrange. If the above configuration does not, try setting :ref:`RC_OPTIONS<RC_OPTIONS>` = 8 which will add padding in the protocol to accommodate this. However, using this option when not required will break operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:68
#: e002b4654bdb43a2866dddbe1b90313a
msgid "Enhanced Configurations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:70
#: dda74b9cfcb34c2d801626e273f832ac
msgid "Since many autopilots have a UART tied to the normal RC input pin for that autopilot which has been disabled, partially or totally, to allow that pins use as a GPIO for RC protocol decodes, including the PWM based ones, several boards now have alternate pin assignment which can be selected with the :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` parameter. This allows the use of those previously disabled UARTs for FPort, without consuming an additional UART."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:72
#: dd20adf20c444badb62ed8086f5a5505
msgid "Several autopilots (e.g. Pixhawkx, Cube, etc.) that use an IOMCU co-processor do not have alternate configurations allowing the use of the RCIN pin. A serial port must be used, as described above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-FPort-receivers.rst:74
#: eec82b5bcde04ee9bf38103108804594
msgid "CUAVv5Nano can use its normal RCinput for FPort. Setup configuration for SERIAL5 for a normal F7/H7 autopilot, as above."
